    },
    {
      "id": "aaab719c-edbb-4c2e-805c-d5b30b0d853c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -208,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 576,
        "height": 176,
        "content": "This workflow receives flight disruption events via webhook, looks up passenger PNR details in a GDS API, uses OpenAI to choose a recovery path, then escalates to Slack or auto-rebooks via HTTP, notifies the passenger by Twilio SMS, and logs outcomes to Google Sheets."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f4dbe8aa-e545-468f-8a45-168e2baceded",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -224,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 640,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "How It Works\n\nReceives a POST webhook with passenger and disruption details (pax_id, tier, itinerary, disruption_type, delay_minutes).\n\nNormalizes the incoming payload and fetches the passenger’s PNR/loyalty context from a GDS API.\n\nSends disruption and PNR details to OpenAI to classify impact, choose a response path, and generate a recommended rebooking option.\n\nRoutes the case to either a VIP concierge escalation, a standard auto-rebooking flow, or a minor-delay notification path based on the OpenAI response.\n\nFor VIP cases, posts an alert to a Slack channel for the concierge desk and sends the passenger an SMS update via Twilio.\n\nFor standard cases, calls the GDS rebooking API with the recommended option, then sends the passenger an SMS update via Twilio.\n\nAppends or updates a row in a Google Sheets \"Disruption Ops Dashboard\" with the passenger, tier, impact score, and chosen response path."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e96f0c3c-80dd-4ce7-9861-4b872a0dd77c",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -208,
        720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 608,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "Setup Steps\n\nConfigure the incoming system to POST disruption events to the workflow’s webhook URL at /trip-disruption.\n\nAdd an OpenAI credential (or API key) for the Disruption Impact Classifier model.\n\nConfigure access to your GDS/loyalty APIs and replace the example api.gds.example.com endpoints with your real lookup and rebooking URLs.\n\nAdd Slack OAuth credentials and set/confirm the target channel (e.g., #vip-recovery-desk).\n\nAdd Twilio credentials, set TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER in your environment, and ensure the webhook payload includes a passenger phone field matching paxPhone.\n\nAdd a Google Sheets OAuth connection, set TRACKER_SHEET_ID in your environment, and ensure the \"Disruption Ops Dashboard\" sheet includes columns for pax_id, tier, impact_score, and response_path."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
